## 11. Conclusion

This project investigated three machine learning and deep learning approaches for music genre classification.

The experimental results showed that SVM achieved the highest song-level classification accuracy (81.50%), followed by Random Forest (78.50%). The CNN achieved 50.00%.

The findings suggest that traditional machine learning approaches outperformed the implemented CNN under the experimental conditions. The project also highlights the importance of song-level data separation in preventing data leakage during model evaluation.

